    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We have RNA-seq from 210 adipose biopsies and a sample table with each person's age and smoking pack-years as numbers. I want to understand which pairs of genes become more or less tightly coordinated as age and smoking go up. This would help us pick candidate pathways for a follow-up cohort."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"which pairs of genes become more or less tightly coordinated as age and smoking go up\" -- available from COBRA. Not stated in your request: COBRA needs more genes than samples -- checked against your files before any run.\n\nSelected path: **COBRA**.\n\n**COBRA** — Model covariate-associated gene co-expression with COBRA. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `design_file`: sample covariate design matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nThis is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
